WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everyone.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.467
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:07.434
You're here. "The Tonight Show."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.667
And happy Halloween, everybody!

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:12.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.934
You can tell I'm in
the Halloween spirit.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.667
I've been wearing my
Jimmy Kimmel costume

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.334
for almost two months now.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:19.567
Well, this is fun.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.767
Earlier tonight, President Biden
and the First Lady

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.734
welcomed trick-or-treaters
to The White House

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:26.667
for the first fully in-person
Halloween celebration

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.167
since the pandemic.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:31.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.801
Yep, Halloween was back at
The White House,

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.667
and it was
a nice chance to reuse

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.734
Melania's Christmas decorations.

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.501
Trick-or-treaters were psyched.

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:46.434
Every kid went home with
a bag of candy.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:48.234
It was different than
the last administration,

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:51.367
when every kid went home with a
bag of classified documents.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.901
[ As Trump ] Only take one.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:55.534
Only take one
classified document.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:59.334
Meet you at Mar-a-Lago."

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:00.667
[ Normal voice ]
I read that some of the

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.234
most popular Halloween candies
this year are

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:05.934
Reese's Peanut Butter Cups,
KitKats, and Snickers.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.801
But there are
some candies out there

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.567
that people don't like as much.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:10.901
Tariq, do you think
you can give us

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.968
some tips on
which candies to avoid?

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:16.000
-Do I? Hit it.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.934
♪♪

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:21.234
♪ Candy corn,
you can take a back seat ♪

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:23.901
♪ You're tacky, waxy,
bad as rancid crab meat ♪

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.868
♪ Necco Wafer,
you're inedible rock ♪

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.501
♪ Just a swole-ass Smartie
that takes like chalk ♪

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:31.033
♪ Don't even get me started on
Good &amp; Plentys ♪

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.667
♪ You taste like pennies,
more like Bad &amp; Too Manys ♪

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:34.801
♪ And Milk Duds? ♪

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:36.234
♪ Get away from me ♪

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.567
♪ Won't get you out of my teeth
until Christmas Eve ♪

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.901
♪ And Jujubes,
you get an ew from me ♪

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.767
♪ I'd rather chew blue cheese
mixed with prune juice, please ♪

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:44.801
♪ And, Dots, how 'bout not? ♪

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.167
♪ You can rot in the box ♪

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.567
♪ Gimme Twix, Junior Mints,
anything but a dot ♪

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.234
♪ Gimme Reese's, Snickers,
Crunch, or Runts ♪

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.434
♪ But gimme Laffy Taffy,
and I'll punch your guts ♪

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:56.033
♪ I'll take anything
out of desperation ♪

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.868
♪ If the only other option
is a box of raisins ♪

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.300
-Oh, come on, now!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.367
Come on. Come on, now.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:08.567
-Oh, my!
-That's amazing.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.534
The greatest!
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.734
-Tariq Trotter! Come on.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.033
Hey, guys, I saw that,
this weekend,

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:21.601
former president Obama
was campaigning in Michigan.

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:23.501
And when he started talking
about getting older,

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:24.934
some women in the crowd
chimed in.

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:26.467
Take a look at this.

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:29.701
-I have to admit that sometimes
going out on the campaign trail

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:32.667
feels a little harder
than it used to.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:36.167
Not just because
I'm older and grayer.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:41.801
-Fine little...
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.200
-I don't know
if y'all heard that.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.667
Said I was still fine.

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.701
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:50.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.067
Fine?

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:54.801
Then Michelle was like,
"Yeah, I think we're done with

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.834
the campaign speeches, alright?"

00:02:56.834 --> 00:03:00.100
He's like, "I'm Barack Obama.
I approved this message."

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.100
That's the one difference
between Obama and Biden.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.667
When Obama is onstage,
people are like, "He is fine."

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:07.701
And when Biden is onstage,
people are like, "He's fine."

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.167
"He's fine."

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:14.167
That's right -- the Democrats
have deployed Obama

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:16.067
on the campaign trail.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.534
Tell me you're nervous
about the midterms

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:20.400
without telling me you're
nervous about the midterms.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.701
Some business news.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.434
In Elon Musk's first round of
layoffs at Twitter,

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:28.567
