25% of the company's workforce.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.834
Meanwhile, Facebook said,
"We're hiring."

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:33.667
Everyone was like, "No, thanks."

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:36.601
But Twitter is actually
trying to hire replacements,

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.334
and we found some questions
on the application

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:39.701
that Elon Musk is sending out.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.167
And here are
some of the questions.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.634
They're very interesting here.
Let's check some of these out.

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:43.834
First one says...

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.300
-Wow!
-Next up, there's...

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.000
After that, it asked...

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:12.601
"V-Bucks, please." Yep.
Then it says...

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.601
These are odd questions.

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:19.767
-Yeah.

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.100
-And, finally, it asks...

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:23.868
-Wow!

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:26.334
-I don't know.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:27.734
Good luck.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.067
But did you see this, though?

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.901
Elon Musk tweeted something that
was considered misinformation

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:34.067
and then deleted it later

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:35.901
because it was
a false conspiracy theory.

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:39.133
Which is awkward when
you're the owner of Twitter.

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.567
Here was the e-mail
that Musk received. It said...

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:04.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's a lot to figure...

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:08.968
Meanwhile, I saw that to reduce
the amount of misinformation

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:10.934
